# Visual consistency for related image sets

When generating **more than one** image/icon/illustration that will appear together (subject covers, profession avatars, store icons, custom-career characters), lock style **before** any generate call. Never generate the set as unrelated one-off prompts.

## Before generating

Write a **Style Lock** and reuse it **verbatim**. It must pin:

- Camera / perspective (exact angle, no mixing)
- Object state (all closed or all open — one decision)
- Light and shadow direction and strength
- Framing (same occupancy of the frame)
- Outline / stroke treatment
- Background: **fully transparent in the shipped PNG** (studio white only as a knockout source). No glued-on opaque plate.

## Preferred generation

One **grid/sheet** of the whole set in a single image, with: “every item is from the same design system, not separate designs.” Split and knock out white afterward (`scripts/knockout-white-bg.py`).

## If generating one-by-one

Paste the **full Style Lock unchanged**. Change **only one variable** (subject name, cover tint, profession). No paraphrasing the lock.

## After generating

Compare side by side. Reject any item that differs in angle, state, scale, or lighting — regenerate that item with the same lock. “Close enough” is not acceptable.

## Example (subject books)

Closed hardcover, 3/4 view ~15° from front-right, key light upper-left, contact shadow down-right, same scale, white knockout background.
